 the label returns zero issues in each project.'","AC-8: 'checked as the final step of the run.'","ABSENCE: the plan never states cleanup executes unconditionally (e.g. in a fixture teardown / try-finally) when a scenario raises or aborts.","Scenarios that mutate-then-assert or abort mid-pass: 'Outbound to both projects', 'Repo-config variety', 'Contamination guard', 'Promote-only'."],"finding":"The cleanup mechanism is specified only as a terminal step ('the run is not considered finished until a follow-up query for the label returns zero'; AC-8 'checked as the final step of the run'), with no statement that it runs on the FAILURE path. Several scenarios create real issues and then assert (e.g. Outbound-to-both, Repo-config variety), and the Contamination-guard and Promote-only scenarios deliberately abort a pass mid-flight. If any assertion fails after issues have been created, a terminal-only cleanup step never executes, leaving real issues stranded in REB/DIG — the exact expensive-to-undo outcome the story exists to prevent.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f18823a7ccb0d28b9","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Cleanup is designed in, not bolted on'; Acceptance Criteria line 8","norm_id":"n9b10be74fef5f37c","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A post-creation assertion fails in the Outbound or Repo-config scenario, leaving created issues live in REB/DIG with cleanup never reached","The suite is interrupted (KeyboardInterrupt/timeout) after creation but before the terminal sweep"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"State in the Approach that cleanup is bound to a teardown that always runs (pytest fixture finalizer / try-finally keyed on the per-run label), and add an acceptance check that a deliberately-failed scenario still leaves zero label-matching issues in both projects.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify crash/error recovery for cleanup: run the label sweep in a teardown/finally that executes even on scenario failure, and document an idempotent standalone re-sweep (by run label) an operator can invoke to reclaim orphans from a crashed run.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T12","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7","T9"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6522,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Cleanup is a single JQL sweep over that label across both live projects, and the run is not considered finished until a follow-up query for the label returns zero issues in each project.'","ABSENCE: no described handling for a crash between issue-creation and the sweep, and no retry/backoff on the Jira API calls the sweep and creation make."],"finding":"The plan creates real issues in live Jira then relies on a single same-run JQL label sweep for cleanup, but does not specify recovery when the run crashes mid-flight (issues created, process dies before the sweep) or when the cleanup sweep itself errors — leaving orphaned live issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fca059bcac4ba09f6","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Cleanup is designed in, not bolted on'; final Acceptance Criterion","norm_id":"n96c7776bd82ba71d","priority":0.2978,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The harness creates issues in REB, then the process is killed (or the Jira API 5xxs) before the label sweep runs, leaving labelled orphans that no later run will clean because each run uses a fresh label."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Wrap issue-creation and the label sweep so the sweep runs in a finally/teardown block regardless of scenario outcome, add bounded retry on the sweep's JQL delete calls, and document in docs/jira-sync-setup.md a manual re-sweep command keyed on the run label for a crashed run.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5556,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State whether the new tests/external/live_multi_project/ harness reuses/extends the existing external-tier confinement (tests/external/conftest.py) and the live_jira_dc store-copy isolation + cleanup primitives (_dc_support.py, test_store_copy_isolation.py), or justify a parallel Cloud-specific implementation.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.535,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Scope: 'tests/external/live_multi_project/ (new) — the rehearsal harness and its scenarios'","Existing prior art: tests/external/conftest.py + tests/unit/test_external_isolation.py enforce the opt-in external tier and hard-fail any external-marked test outside tests/external/","Existing prior art: tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_store_copy_isolation.py implements asserted (not assumed) store-copy isolation with layered precondition checks; its docstring: 'Keeping a second copy here would reproduce, inside this suite, the duplicated-and-drifted defect class the epic is fixing elsewhere'","Existing prior art: tests/external/live_jira_dc/_dc_support.py + conftest.py centralize per-run keying, store-copy fixtures, and cleanup helpers","The plan's own precondition-assertion posture ('asserts the configured remote is the S3 copy and not the production remote') closely mirrors the DC harness's layered isolation assertions"],"finding":"The plan introduces a new live-external harness (tests/external/live_multi_project/) with its own isolation precondition assertion, dry-run gating, and run-scoped-label cleanup, but does not acknowledge or propose reusing the repo's existing, established prior art for exactly these mechanisms: the tests/external/ tier-confinement machinery (conftest auto-marker + REBAR_RUN_EXTERNAL opt-in + collection-time confinement hard-fail) and the live-Jira store-copy isolation harness under tests/external/live_jira_dc/ (test_store_copy_isolation.py, _dc_support.py, shared conftest fixtures). Reimplementing these from scratch risks the very 'duplicated-and-drifted' defect class that harness's own docstring records the team already fixed by centralizing helpers.","group_criteria":null,"group_id